  "issue": "### Language Support Missing for Certain Languages\n\n#### Description\n\nIt seems that some languages are no longer supported in the latest update. Specifically, when attempting to use certain languages, the expected output is not generated. This issue arises when trying to generate audio files for languages that were previously supported.\n\n#### How to Reproduce\n\n1. Set up the environment as per the project documentation.\n2. Attempt to generate an audio file using the `gTTS` library for the following languages:\n   - Amharic\n   - Welsh\n   - Basque\n   - French (Canada)\n   - Galician\n   - Hausa\n   - Lithuanian\n   - Punjabi (Gurmukhi)\n\nExample code snippet:\n\n```python\nfrom gtts import gTTS\n\ntext = \"This is a test\"\nlang = \"am\"  # Replace with any of the languages listed above\ntts = gTTS(text=text, lang=lang, slow=False)\ntts.save(\"output.mp3\")\n```\n\n3. Check the output file size or existence.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe audio file should be successfully created for all supported languages, with a file size greater than 1500 bytes.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nThe audio file is not created for the specified languages, or the file size is unexpectedly small.\n\n#### Additional Context\n\nThis issue might be related to recent changes in the language support configuration. Please verify the language codes and ensure all previously supported languages are included.",
